# Static files (must be before SPA fallback handled by CF Pages by default)

# Google asks for its verification file at the .html path it issued.
#
# Pages serves static assets before it reads this file, and it strips .html
# from any asset that has it -- so while a real google....html sat here, the
# .html path answered 308 to the extension-less one and the self-rewrite that
# was meant to force a 200 never got a look in.
#
# With the file named .htm there is no asset at the .html path for Pages to
# normalise, so the rewrite runs. .htm rather than .txt so Google still
# receives the content type the file was issued as.
/google4fb6a85272b47cc5.html  /google4fb6a85272b47cc5.htm  200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200
/robots.txt  /robots.txt  200
